# Consumption order for HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M.
#
# Read from the Llama forward pass, not guessed. Per layer:
#
#   h = x + o_proj(attn(q_proj(rms(x)), k_proj(rms(x)), v_proj(rms(x))))
#   y = h + down_proj(silu(gate_proj(rms(h))) * up_proj(rms(h)))
#
# so the seven weight matrices are consumed q, k, v, o, gate, up, down.
#
# THE FIRST NON-RECURSIVE RUNG. TRM, HRM and BDH each re-read one small
# weight set many times per forward; SmolLM has 30 distinct layers and
# reads each weight exactly ONCE. There is no rotation and no rewind
# inside a forward pass -- the [rotating] section below is swept once
# and rewound only between forwards.
#
# That is not a worse fit for this architecture. It is a better one.
# A single forward is 210 streams read strictly in order, start to
# finish, with no re-reads at all: the ideal sequential workload.
# What recursion bought the earlier rungs was a small working set, not
# reuse -- see docs/results.md, saga 2 step 8.
#
# [resident] IS 21% OF THIS MODEL, and that is the rung's cost.
# SmolLM ties its embeddings: `model.embed_tokens.weight` is both the
# input lookup and the output projection, 28,311,552 weights against
# 134,515,008 total. An embedding is gathered by token id, so it
# cannot be swept to serve one token, and it stays in RAM.
#
# Compare 0.13% resident for TRM and 0.05% for HRM. A research model
# with a tiny vocabulary flatters this architecture; a real language
# model with a 49,152-token vocabulary does not. The streamable
# fraction is 79%.
#
# The 61 RMS norm scales are 1-D and total 35,136 weights, 0.03%.
# They are resident for the same reason TRM's are: streaming them
# would be silly.

[rotating]
model.layers.0.self_attn.q_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.k_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.v_proj.weight
model.layers.0.self_attn.o_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.gate_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.up_proj.weight
model.layers.0.mlp.down_proj.weight
